<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17059" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀτημέλ-ητος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>unheeded, unnoticed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				5.4.18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.1.14
			</span></i>, and so prob. in <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				891
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-τως, ἔχειν</span> to be <i>uncared for,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Cyr.</u>
				8.1.15
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>slovenly,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀ. τοὺς κικίννους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alciphr.
					3.55
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ἀ. τῶν τριχῶν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Mis.</u>
					365d
				</span></i>
			.</div>
